  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182550/assets/ec14b1461a3125c2b4c320166230980ee33cbd004e07692e2c7763868f0edaa1.png)\n\nWhat is the measure of $\\overset{―}{OC}$ if $AB=15?$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the points $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ lie on the circle. From the diagram, the radius of the circle is $r=OC.$ \n\nWe first notice that\n\n$$\nAB=AO+OB.\n$$\n\nNow, $\\overset{―}{AO}$ and $\\overset{―}{OB}$ are both segments between the center of the circle and the circle itself. So, they are both radii of the circle, and because $AB=15,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =15 \\\\ AO+OB & =15 \\\\ r+r & =15 \\\\ 2r & =15 \\\\ r & =7.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\nOC=r=7.5.\n$$",
